+# BLOCKED: contradictory underscore requirements in test_slug.py
+
+## What is blocked
+
+`test_slug.py` cannot be made to pass in full without editing the tests. Two
+tests assert **different expected outputs for the exact same input**:
+
+| Test | Input | Expected output |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `test_preserves_underscores` (line 24) | `"user_id field"` | `"user_id-field"` |
+| `test_underscores_become_dashes` (line 28) | `"user_id field"` | `"user-id-field"` |
+
+`slugify` is a pure function of its input. For the single input
+`"user_id field"` it can only return one string, so it can satisfy at most one
+of these two assertions. No implementation — and no change to `slug.py` that
+leaves the tests untouched — can make both pass.
+
+## Why it is not a work-aroundable problem
+
+The two tests encode mutually exclusive rules:
+
+* `test_preserves_underscores` cites **Spec 4.2**: identifiers keep their
+  underscores, i.e. underscores are preserved as-is.
+* `test_underscores_become_dashes` cites **Spec 4.5**: slugs only ever contain
+  `[a-z0-9-]`, i.e. underscores must be converted to dashes.
+
+Both cannot hold for the same character in the same input. This is a
+contradiction in the content team's URL spec itself (or in how the tests
+transcribe it), not a bug in the implementation. Since the tests are the source
+of truth and must not be changed, resolving it requires a spec owner to decide
+which rule wins.
+
+Any attempt to special-case the tests (e.g. branching on the exact input
+string, call order, or test name) would be a workaround that makes the suite
+green while leaving the behaviour undefined, so it was not done.
+
+## What was done instead
+
+`slug.py` was implemented to satisfy every non-contradictory test. The
+underscore behaviour was chosen as **preserve underscores** (Spec 4.2), because
+punctuation stripping should not consume a word character and that keeps
+identifier-style titles round-trippable. With that choice:
+
+* 6 of 7 tests pass (`test_lowercase_and_spaces`, `test_strips_punctuation`,
+  `test_collapses_dashes`, `test_accents`, `test_trims`,
+  `test_preserves_underscores`).
+* `test_underscores_become_dashes` fails, as it necessarily must.
+
+Current result:
+
+```
+$ python3 -m unittest test_slug
+Ran 7 tests
+FAILED (failures=1)
+```
+
+Flipping the choice (converting `_` to `-`) passes the other six and makes
+`test_preserves_underscores` the sole failure instead. There is no third
+option.
+
+## Decision needed
+
+The content team/spec owner needs to resolve Spec 4.2 vs Spec 4.5 for
+underscores. Once one rule is chosen, the other test should be corrected or
+removed, and the one-line regex in `slugify` adjusted accordingly.
